    "problem_statement": "Err.and_then returns wrong value when called on Err instance\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen calling `and_then` on an `Err` instance, it returns the operation function instead of the original `Err` instance.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom result import Err, Ok\n\ndef square(x):\n    return Ok(x * x)\n\n# This should return the original Err(3), but returns the function instead\nerr_result = Err(3)\nresult = err_result.and_then(square)\nprint(f\"Expected: Err(3), Got: {result}\")\n```\n\nThe `and_then` method on `Err` instances should return `self` (the original error) since there's no value to transform, but it's currently returning the operation function passed to it."
  }
